", "title": "Production literacy", "children": [{"id": "d72fab86-76db-4cf5-bf4d-9b0faac6090e", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot, scene, sequence, take, coverage, slate, call sheet, dailies, rough cut, fine cut, and final export"}, {"id": "18a012d2-e9b0-4e11-851d-86eb65fca511", "type": "concept", "title": "File formats, codecs, frame rates, aspect ratios, and project settings"}, {"id": "37d9a5aa-5b14-4cf8-8265-5c40d5225c42", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional habits: labeling, backups, shared folders, and version control"}], "description": "The goal is to make students conversant in the basic vocabulary, tools, and standards of media-making."}]}, {"id": "66fef562-af5c-475e-9133-df9f3e8b2d68", "type": "topic", "title": "Visual Storytelling, Shot Grammar, and Composition", "description": "Learn how framing, shot choice, movement, and visual continuity communicate story, tone, and meaning.", "children": [{"id": "1f81ed18-e244-4260-90f7-487578feddeb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shot types and visual grammar", "children": [{"id": "dd16e909-3a3e-4271-bcf3-e48e008ef194", "type": "concept", "title": "Extreme wide, wide, medium, close-up, insert, cutaway, over-the-shoulder, and point-of-view shots"}, {"id": "e7e19502-adb0-456a-b934-82b49fe946c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Establishing shots, reactions, eyeline matches, and screen direction"}, {"id": "1f05761c-0ea5-4224-9b7a-17aff27013f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuity, axis of action, and the 180-degree rule"}], "description": "Shot grammar helps students understand how image choices guide attention, emotion, and story comprehension."}, {"id": "219c4666-b849-4935-9f57-b1b71758b0bc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Composition and frame design", "children": [{"id": "a75167c4-63df-4bbd-8fa0-ebf73ce15076", "type": "concept", "title": "Rule of thirds, balance, symmetry, negative space, depth, foreground, middle ground, and background"}, {"id": "28003886-e938-4125-91be-59f7d9fcad79", "type": "concept", "title": "Headroom, lead room, frame edges, blocking, and movement through the frame"}, {"id": "a93bad3c-f908-4ba7-90a5-87b3535def77", "type": "concept", "title": "Color, shape, texture, line, contrast, and visual hierarchy"}], "description": "Composition turns a camera image into a deliberate arrangement of meaning and emphasis."}, {"id": "74b0d55c-32cc-4a3e-b13d-26e0671babb7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Storyboards, shot lists, and visual plans", "children": [{"id": "f89f7c63-23d8-45b6-bc0a-6befe9939c68", "type": "concept", "title": "Storyboards, overhead diagrams, shot lists, mood boards, and look references"}, {"id": "f61fa1cb-07c6-4ba1-baad-b3d1a5724e90", "type": "concept", "title": "Coverage strategy for action, dialogue, interviews, demonstrations, and B-roll"}, {"id": "1256db88-cb7e-4f79-8045-66a2568b4a26", "type": "concept", "title": "Matching visual ambition to available time, crew, locations, and equipment"}], "description": "Planning visual coverage before the shoot helps students make creative choices under time pressure."}]}, {"id": "4b9c0f7d-0355-4954-b823-9c01436ebea3", "type": "topic", "title": "Camera Operation, Exposure, Lenses, and Image Control", "description": "Build practical camera literacy so technical settings become deliberate storytelling choices.", "children": [{"id": "fdb35ac9-aa80-47cd-8444-5135e8affcd2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Camera fundamentals", "children": [{"id": "04ded620-cb6b-4e75-9f71-fcc7795e1a09", "type": "concept", "title": "Camera bodies, sensors, menus, media cards, batteries, tripods, stabilizers, and monitors"}, {"id": "22bac8eb-bbd7-452c-b800-cc69ff171b9b", "type": "concept", "title": "Resolution, frame rate, shutter speed, ISO, white balance, and picture profiles"}, {"id": "b922d5b1-6bad-4ba6-9da9-aa4516afb800", "type": "concept", "title": "Focus, zoom, stabilization, handheld work, and basic camera movement"}], "description": "Students learn the camera as a controllable image-making system rather than a point-and-record device."}, {"id": "9c906e88-000c-48e6-a288-7c7bac8b6d23", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exposure and image quality", "children": [{"id": "94738a72-2910-4168-ae82-d3672142d48f", "type": "concept", "title": "Aperture, shutter, ISO, neutral density, zebras, histograms, false color, and waveform basics"}, {"id": "d57014b7-98e7-4e7c-ab0d-62b87c09ce4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Dynamic range, highlights, shadows, noise, clipping, and underexposure"}, {"id": "2a9ee1b5-9f27-4e24-8ebd-8927cd373e3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Natural light, mixed light, available light, and practical exposure decisions"}], "description": "Exposure literacy lets students create usable images and understand tradeoffs among brightness, motion, noise, and depth of field."}, {"id": "d2fc80bb-7930-441b-b921-ed2c44c962dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lenses and perspective", "children": [{"id": "7e352ef3-2c51-4fd0-89a7-fefddee9381d", "type": "concept", "title": "Focal length, field of view, lens compression, distortion, minimum focus, and depth of field"}, {"id": "07e9c1f0-8cee-4b57-9d82-317dd488c9eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Prime versus zoom lenses, macro, wide, normal, telephoto, and specialty lenses"}, {"id": "8b3957f8-15e3-4080-a859-5415d95233a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Matching lens decisions to subject, genre, location, and blocking"}], "description": "Lens choice shapes how space, faces, motion, and emotional distance feel on screen."}]}, {"id": "899beb34-f351-45a5-a151-15d33cce3370", "type": "topic", "title": "Lighting Fundamentals and Visual Mood", "description": "Use light direction, quality, contrast, color, and safety to shape visibility, emotion, and space.", "children": [{"id": "93c5e6c7-eb38-4411-aa51-c21a841a89c2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Qualities of light", "children": [{"id": "8f0c9223-3b8b-4277-8bc6-84f3fc5a3a32", "type": "concept", "title": "Hard and soft light, direction, intensity, falloff, contrast, color temperature, and motivation"}, {"id"