ack notes, and locking a production draft"}], "description": "Different formats help teams understand different kinds of media projects."}, {"id": "8db52d4e-4811-47af-a859-255efa012820", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Script breakdown", "children": [{"id": "e9b25618-ae4b-49c9-a7b2-a8693bf20f67", "type": "concept", "title": "Cast, locations, props, wardrobe, set dressing, vehicles, effects, sound needs, and special equipment"}, {"id": "9721b44d-634e-4089-97b5-45078f2c1590", "type": "concept", "title": "Coverage planning, scene priorities, pages-per-day, and scheduling implications"}, {"id": "9907d67a-ae63-4e90-a642-c0f1946f44ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Identifying legal, ethical, safety, accessibility, and budget concerns"}], "description": "Breaking down the script connects writing to the real needs of production."}]}, {"id": "9b249788-9d01-4f4b-98c7-b7c8d2831498", "type": "topic", "title": "Directing, Blocking, Performance, and On-Set Communication", "description": "Practice directing actors, subjects, crew, camera, and action with clear communication and ethical leadership.", "children": [{"id": "445add86-2b72-41c9-b310-0716b8a6200b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Directing actors and participants", "children": [{"id": "22a9855b-ec36-4311-b4f6-632f1be84196", "type": "concept", "title": "Objectives, beats, playable actions, adjustments, rehearsal, improvisation, and listening"}, {"id": "d87babfc-7ff7-4df6-85c4-88e008743122", "type": "concept", "title": "Working with non-actors, interview subjects, children, communities, and vulnerable participants"}, {"id": "4de856b5-e323-4659-9604-7b82cf344c2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, comfort, boundaries, and trauma-aware communication"}], "description": "Directing is about creating conditions where people can give truthful, usable performances or testimony."}, {"id": "56ddb8d5-743a-4c2e-9ba6-f8ad0f6870ad", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Blocking and staging", "children": [{"id": "8406d76a-dd3b-437f-86e7-f4c2ff43f1f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Entrances, exits, marks, eyelines, camera movement, actor movement, and props"}, {"id": "6c7286da-3085-4135-a2c5-97d262ae7fd7", "type": "concept", "title": "Blocking for continuity, motivated movement, tension, and emotional focus"}, {"id": "7c080144-a6f6-48e9-89bd-1bb4b222292e", "type": "concept", "title": "Staging interviews, demonstrations, documentary action, and group scenes"}], "description": "Blocking connects bodies, camera, light, sound, and space into a coherent scene."}, {"id": "19b55855-71b8-4223-aee1-38e0a71520af", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Set communication", "children": [{"id": "5ddcce82-15d2-43c1-b8ca-60467f12eb57", "type": "concept", "title": "Calls, resets, quiet on set, rolling, cut, pickups, notes, and department communication"}, {"id": "10d610c0-c9ea-4bf5-bde2-2703d09017f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Giving concise direction, receiving crew feedback, and resolving conflicts"}, {"id": "a18bf2f7-2344-4df7-a05b-a9e974c3ac53", "type": "concept", "title": "Leadership habits: respect, clarity, inclusion, punctuality, and accountability"}], "description": "Good on-set communication preserves time, morale, safety, and creative clarity."}]}, {"id": "3e3304ae-cd56-47bc-930a-fb00f6a07e92", "type": "topic", "title": "Documentary and Nonfiction Production Basics", "description": "Introduce research, interviews, observation, verite practice, archival material, consent, and truthful nonfiction structure.", "children": [{"id": "cc1a3ce2-b104-4246-a767-cb3520e4cc39", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research and access", "children": [{"id": "517a19da-9761-47a0-a02b-56e24ea75eb2", "type": "concept", "title": "Topic research, participant outreach, access negotiations, background reading, and archival discovery"}, {"id": "621a672d-9952-46a0-8776-8e445fd831d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical framing, positionality, consent, transparency, and participant expectations"}, {"id": "d32a3f69-ceeb-472b-b9da-b03ed71057a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning for actuality, interviews, verite, reenactment, and archival media"}], "description": "Nonfiction projects depend on trust, preparation, and a clear reason for filming."}, {"id": "febfa04e-209d-463c-9efa-0942136d8737", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interview and observation", "children": [{"id": "11e7f1d0-b0b8-4280-872b-96adf03b2ae4", "type": "concept", "title": "Interview questions, listening, follow-up prompts, silence, room setup, eye line, and release forms"}, {"id": "09ebbab9-c354-4bdc-ab91-268b9cd5682e", "type": "concept", "title": "Observational shooting, B-roll, sequences, action coverage, and environmental sound"}, {"id": "49991197-f780-4297-a49b-83c06db8c467", "type": "concept", "title": "Working in real locations with changing light, sound, time, and participant comfort"}], "description": "Students practice capturing unscripted material with technical control and human sensitivity."}, {"id": "60dc6a1d-aba0-48ab-8983-51a3c7285099", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nonfiction structure", "children": [{"id": "60569e27-60f9-4cd7-82be-0b096cf61154", "type": "concept", "title": "Character, conflict, theme, argument, chronology, essay structure, and process structure"}, {"id": "85b7fa6c-69e0-44ce-bbc2-10f45f97d894", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice-over, text cards, archival material, evidence, and fair representation"}, {"id": "b9923e3c-53d1-4fd5-ac9b-a8eae8e6c9f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountability to participants, audience, and truth claims"}], "description": "Documentary editing begins before the shoot through research questions and story hypotheses."}]}, {"id": "b060f3e6-e215-4ac2-8996-840764c52c27", "type": "topic", "title": "Editing Software, Continuity, and Post-Production Workflow", "description": "Organize media, build assemblies, shape continuity, manage versions, and develop editorial judgment in modern NLEs.", "children": [{"id": "7539f935-dbe7-4f85-8128-c0dfc625186c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "NLE foundations", "children": [{"id": "e19449d5-f282-42d2-8322-298a32bf28ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve, Final Cut, or comparable NLE workspace basics"}, {"id": "984660c9-5825-457e-bd28-3e39c0e9055d", "type": "concept", "title": "Ingest, bins, metadata, markers, syncing, multicam basics, timelines, and project settings"}, {"id": "16c869d8-276b-43ac-a3f5-5c193ce1ad40", "type": "concept", "title": "Proxy workflow, relinking, backups, autosaves, versioning, and exports"}], "description": "Students learn to operate editing software with organized, repeatable workflow rather than trial-and-error clutter."}, {"id": "48729378-93d9-4745-961b-b8a276f8eca5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Continuity and story editing", "children": [{"id": "272432f1-f285-4223-a0e8-ea30f9c8c899", "type": "concept", "title": "Assembly, rough cut, fine cut, picture lock, continuity, pacing, rhythm, and clarity"}, {"id": "ba4d845d-1104-4f7d-a381-f9edd763d4c5", "type": "concept", "title": "J-cuts, L-cuts, match cuts, cutaways, reaction shots, montage, and ellipsis"}, {"id": "3f1fc41e-51fe-4b2b-81ca-fbaf41d6e826", "type": "concept", "title": "Performance selection, scene beats, transitions, and audience attention"}], "description": "Editing teaches students to shape material into coherent time, space, emotion, and meaning."}, {"id": "1a52a448-f19f-410b-9944-96482489aa6a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Collaboration and review", "children": [{"id": "9c3ae630-0f72-45a7-9d08-e61ee4e6adee", "type": "concept", "title": "Exporting review cuts, naming versions, receiving notes, spotting issues, and making revision logs"}, {"id": "25096440-e2e8-4f75-b148-dc369867a5a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Working with directors, producers, sound editors, colorists, and peers"}, {"id": "21d75487-b584-40d0-bbd4-0e619dac31ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding common problems: lost media, mixed frame rates, weak backups, and unclear file names"}], "description": "Post-production is a collaborative process of notes, revisions, and disciplined decision-making."}]}, {"id": "8a7edb6b-ac20-4793-ada9-e86324441284", "type": "topic", "title": "Sound Editing, Music, Color, Graphics, and Finishing", "description": "Move beyond assembly into polished finishing through audio, color, titles, export settings, and quality control.", "children": [{"id": "2b6fcd7d-b843-4524-a323-7ebac8cef16a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sound post-production", "children": [{"id": "ee480901-2d28-42e3-b53a-e677408c10a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Dialogue editing, noise reduction, room tone, ambience, Foley, effects, music, levels, and basic mixing"}, {"id": "ab1d3529-01d0-4e51-b0df-fa1f88c57a33", "type": "concept", "title": "Sound bridges, perspective, offscreen sound, silence, and emotional rhythm"}, {"id": "4585c6d8-1f90-47d2-bb14-6e0c3aa1b398", "type": "concept", "title": "Loudness targets, stereo export, headphones versus speakers, and quality checks"}], "description": "Sound finishing adds clarity, space, continuity, emotion, and polish."}, {"id": "25f388e8-db06-4100-a277-d8fcf319c565", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color and image finishing", "children": [{"id": "45cfc41d-4be4-4b9e-902c-711f177e595e", "type": "concept", "title": "Color correction, white balance fixes, exposure matching, scopes, contrast, saturation, skin tone, and shot matching"}, {"id": "599d4fff-7b70-487e-9859-fa90b7d28bb9", "type": "concept", "title": "Creative looks, LUTs, consistency, restraint, and avoiding overcorrection"}, {"id": "178b3c6f-e93d-4f1a-8f0b-ba228aab806a", "type": "concept", "title": "Graphics, titles, captions, credits, lower thirds, and motion basics"}], "description": "Color work helps shots match, images feel intentional, and exports meet platform expectations."}, {"id": "bbeeb212-a83c-49c3-bb4b-3351f546a3fe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Export and quality control", "children": [{"id": "41a08f53-e074-47db-a4ad-2b22becc8b2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Codec, container, bitrate, resolution, frame rate, audio settings, captions, thumbnails, and stills"}, {"id": "92df25a7-41ec-4740-bcbc-73fce313226d", "type": "concept", "title": "Checking sync, spelling, levels, legal credits, dead frames, glitches, and compression artifacts"}, {"id": "01ce7a83-2a67-4561-a534-ffad9b8f6acc", "type": "concept", "title": "Archiving project files, masters, web exports, captions, releases, and production stills"}], "description": "Finishing is where creative work becomes a reliable deliverable."}]}, {"id": "243c16ba-d73e-4f28-9f8c-09c7eac033d8", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics, Safety, Copyright, Releases, and Inclusive Production", "description": "Build responsible habits around people, locations, law, representation, accessibility, and set safety.", "children": [{"id": "ba693d70-cd43-4cef-924b-780608c18803", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical production practice", "children": [{"id": "557c5fff-74a5-486c-ab91-d59a6a9f1464", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, representation, power, privacy, dignity, context, and harm reduction"}, {"id": "b0e35f7b-0507-448e-9bb4-7b5daf745b6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Working with communities, vulnerable subjects, sensitive topics, and public spaces"}, {"id": "8844a8d2-d6d7-4d1e-8e6f-798f0615eca1", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountability in documentary, fiction, branded, campus, and social media projects"}], "description": "Students learn that media production affects real people and communities, not only images on a screen."}, {"id": "6f85258a-921a-4302-a273-9a69839fb443", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Legal and rights basics", "children": [{"id": "97baf529-bd10-440a-baf4-0ae0e82519f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Talent releases, location releases, music rights, archival rights, fair use, Creative Commons, public domain, and trademarks"}, {"id": "fcbc3fd8-bbf1-49fe-bcc7-23554355eaf6", "type": "concept", "title": "Credits, contracts, ownership, collaboration agreements, and distribution permissions"}, {"id": "1d4d