ed by who the work is for and how they will encounter it."}, {"id": "cf9cf572-bbc4-461f-b834-8e9a8e25c103", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Festival and professional presentation", "children": [{"id": "87008bdd-8c21-46ed-a0a0-0aed95a3cbb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Festival strategy, submission platforms, deadlines, premiere status, screening copies, stills, synopsis, logline, director statement, and bio"}, {"id": "5fd93601-e558-4ad1-bb62-893a1ec6df01", "type": "concept", "title": "Press kits, posters, trailers, social assets, and public-facing project descriptions"}, {"id": "187267c0-994c-4b67-af3d-3471625432a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical promotion, participant approval, and expectation management"}], "description": "Students learn the basics of presenting work beyond the classroom."}, {"id": "91b6a90d-bbdc-4212-bd60-565b04d693df", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio and career readiness", "children": [{"id": "964ce887-5819-4c7d-a040-33cb3ddc8072", "type": "concept", "title": "Reel selection, project page, process notes, credits, role clarity, and reflective artist statement"}, {"id": "ba24867f-a31e-4eff-a3ee-cbdbcc2ed5cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Networking, collaboration records, recommendation materials, and professional communication"}, {"id": "19dd9b2b-a70e-4e1a-a8d3-79d786f5ef62", "type": "concept", "title": "Archiving masters, documentation, production stills, behind-the-scenes images, and release paperwork"}], "description": "Delivery also means preparing evidence of skill for internships, jobs, grants, and future coursework."}]}, {"id": "b539fe89-d731-4b31-90a0-b607d6bb9c7f", "type": "topic", "title": "Critique, Revision, Collaboration, and Production Portfolio", "description": "Use critique, reflection, peer collaboration, and revision to strengthen the final project and professional portfolio.", "children": [{"id": "59055e83-6b66-4699-9c47-124f4079d4ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critique literacy", "children": [{"id": "16d46ffe-e87f-43e0-be41-7611cbd6ff9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive feedback, interpretive feedback, evaluative feedback, and actionable notes"}, {"id": "0cd6f566-9b6e-463d-9f3a-3952b2cd4b01", "type": "concept", "title": "Separating intention, execution, audience response, and technical issue"}, {"id": "348b12f3-a7d0-42cb-80a6-17406237f1cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Using evidence from the work rather than vague preference"}], "description": "Critique turns feedback into better creative judgment when students know how to give and receive it."}, {"id": "d57e30a7-c69b-4c95-8660-6846021915ed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revision strategy", "children": [{"id": "f349ebd3-2aa0-4cc9-8c12-33280a8700f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Note triage, revision logs, alternate cuts, test screenings, and deadlines"}, {"id": "4611094b-33ff-4aca-87f4-f99364e07891", "type": "concept", "title": "Fixing story, structure, pacing, audio, color, graphics, credits, and export problems"}, {"id": "a3e2beda-9cea-4dc4-9bc5-0578b8cbfeea", "type": "concept", "title": "Knowing when to reshoot, rerecord, rewrite, cut, simplify, or finish"}], "description": "Revision helps students prioritize the changes that most improve clarity, emotion, ethics, and finish."}, {"id": "606cb656-c03b-4fe9-bce0-939bbd099f9d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Collaborative professionalism", "children": [{"id": "68602561-5e76-42f0-b207-ae8785f57f19", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer roles, accountability, credits, conflict resolution, shared folders, and meeting notes"}, {"id": "d405b7c2-3499-4589-92bb-81475ac1050b", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflective memos on creative decisions, constraints, and lessons learned"}, {"id": "fb3d140b-0c9c-4487-904a-9b668146a8a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio assembly, role descriptions, and evidence of process"}], "description": "The course should build habits students can carry into advanced production and creative work."}]}, {"id": "53ca652b-6e98-4779-be8b-4d505603f2c8", "type": "topic", "title": "Final Short Media Project Capstone", "description": "Synthesize the course by developing, shooting, editing, finishing, and presenting a short media work.", "children": [{"id": "76937584-4e5b-41f6-8c13-0984385dfb75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project proposal and greenlight", "children": [{"id": "5a01625e-71c1-4932-8129-dfb270a6f20c", "type": "concept", "title": "Logline, treatment, audience, aesthetic references, schedule, budget, roles, and risk plan"}, {"id": "8bc0e6b8-b275-41e9-8947-61c16421795f", "type": "concept", "title": "Script, storyboard, shot list, interview plan, location plan, release plan, and equipment list"}, {"id": "2ed4123d-4e18-44e0-86fa-6e6efe4346f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Instructor or peer greenlight based on feasibility, ethics, safety, and learning goals"}], "description": "The capstone begins with a clear, feasible idea that can be evaluated before production starts."}, {"id": "aa35aa9f-6748-4630-a593-ebc0bfeed889", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Production and post-production execution", "children": [{"id": "dc9d88a4-0e7c-44b0-b466-3665f9b3de07", "type": "concept", "title": "Principal photography, sound recording, lighting, directing, production notes, backups, and dailies"}, {"id": "cbac1c3d-42cf-4a29-a0ca-759e1063a632", "type": "concept", "title": "Assembly, rough cut, fine cut, picture lock, sound edit, color, titles, captions, and final export"}, {"id": "1395485e-dc32-4f57-b876-ed0b12274a99", "type": "concept", "title": "Technical quality control, credits, archive package, and delivery specifications"}], "description": "Students synthesize camera, sound, lighting, directing, producing, editing, and finishing in one complete work."}, {"id": "d8c43f20-438a-4b65-8fb9-ea0ba434676d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Screening, reflection, and portfolio package", "children": [{"id": "e6d6769d-b8d2-4e4b-ba49-472aa1e572de", "type": "concept", "title": "Public or class screening, critique, artist statement, production reflection, and revision note"}, {"id": "8d008c5f-bd6b-4f5e-93c0-c0c1bd20aff1", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio page, thumbnail, stills, credits, synopsis, role description, and release documentation"}, {"id": "a3d61ffb-69af-4e32-9810-2be7a342dc70", "type": "concept", "title": "Next-step plan for festivals, web release, reshoots, advanced coursework, or portfolio refinement"}], "description": "The final step is presenting the work, learning from response, and turning the project into future evidence."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$impdjson$::jsonb,
